    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Hatfield Cemetery, listed on the National Register of Historic Places, is located just a half-mile from Sarah Ann.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarah_ann_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sarah Ann sits in a narrow valley along Island Creek, a tributary of the Guyandotte River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarah_ann_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The landscape around Sarah Ann features rugged terrain with steep slopes and deeply incised valleys formed by stream erosion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarah_ann_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Forested hills dominated by oak, hickory, and yellow-poplar cover about eighty percent of the Sarah Ann area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sarah_ann_west_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Historical strip mining has impacted the local ecology of Sarah Ann through acid mine drainage in Island Creek.",
